From 577bf92c88eae86d7dfff02df3606dbd6657bab8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 15:37:30 +0800
Subject: [caplifive-buildroot PATCH 3/4] Raise the buddy allocator's maximum
 order so interpreter images fit a domain

A domain region is one __get_free_pages() allocation covering the code image,
DOMAIN_DATA_SIZE and headroom of max(2 * code_len, 512 KiB), so the buddy
allocator's maximum order is a hard ceiling on domain image size. At the default
MAX_ORDER of 11 the largest region is 4 MiB and code_len cannot exceed
1,376,256 bytes. Setting 13 gives a 16 MiB largest block and lifts that to
5,570,560 bytes.

This is what a JerryScript domain needs: its image is 2,965,680 bytes, so the
region has to be order 12, two orders above what the default allows. MicroPython
already sits close to the old ceiling.

The kernel side of this is a companion commit on components/linux, which adds
the ARCH_FORCE_MAX_ORDER symbol to arch/riscv -- without it this line is silently
dropped by olddefconfig instead of taking effect. Both directions were checked,
and the running kernel now shows 13 order columns in /proc/buddyinfo with free
blocks at order 12.

Blast radius is small: pageblock_order comes from HUGETLB_PAGE_ORDER (9) rather
than MAX_ORDER-1 here, so it is unchanged, and the memory model is FLATMEM, which
has no section-size interaction to violate. A small control domain still runs
after the change.
---
 components/linux      | 2 +-
 configs/kernel.config | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/linux b/components/linux
index 830b3c6..5a07050 160000
--- a/components/linux
+++ b/components/linux
@@ -1 +1 @@
-Subproject commit 830b3c68c1fb1e9176028d02ef86f3cf76aa2476
+Subproject commit 5a07050d2228ba7ae71100081284474d809561e8
diff --git a/configs/kernel.config b/configs/kernel.config
index 086587c..dd43704 100644
--- a/configs/kernel.config
+++ b/configs/kernel.config
@@ -30,6 +30,10 @@ CONFIG_SOC_SIFIVE=y
 CONFIG_SOC_STARFIVE=y
 CONFIG_SOC_VIRT=y
 CONFIG_SMP=y
+# Domain regions are one __get_free_pages() allocation, so the buddy allocator
+# caps the domain image size. 13 => largest block 2^12 pages = 16 MiB, which
+# lifts the maximum domain code_len from 1,376,256 to 5,570,560 bytes.
+CONFIG_ARCH_FORCE_MAX_ORDER=13
 CONFIG_HOTPLUG_CPU=y
 CONFIG_PM=y
 CONFIG_CPU_IDLE=y
